caseFoot n=9999: Odds: the game’s own. Values: collected sale medians, 45,060 sales across 1040 of 1810 rolls (57%). Break: how often that tier is worth dismantling rather than listing. Each piece counts at whichever is worth more, under the same bar the Sort tab uses, so this assumes you sort every piece rather than listing all of them. The case order book could not fill the whole purchase, so the cost shown is a floor. Selling what you open moves these prices, and the more you open at once the more it moves them.
caseSwing n=9999: One case swings 7.06 either way against an edge of 0.090 — about 24,400 cases before profit reliably beats the swing. Below that a losing run is normal, not evidence the edge is wrong.
